              ":question/id": "b2196eb1-6691-549b-950a-a9bab6863a70",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4683",
              ":question/problem": "What is the coefficient matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=1 \\\\ 2y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "First, we organize the system so that every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=1 \\\\ 0x+2y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n\t\t1 & -2  \\\\\n\t\t0 & 2 \n\t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "cb13e9d9-19f0-5f39-b9f8-e6e2f8fac433",
